From c5aac2237cd5d1334071e31d02016f77c7305930 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Sun, 02 Nov 2026 20:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] rdna-boosts: block 17: RDNA2 (gfx1030) FA prefill -- the q_global threshold and the D=256 ncols2 cap lift

On gfx1030 (RDNA2) the flash-attention TILE kernel is ~15-16% slower than
the stock kernel at long context (pp2048 @ d32768: 1041.0 vs 1231.7 t/s on
Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, head-256 GQA-8, -lm dio -b 8192 -ub 2048 -fa 1).  The
regression is in the block-05 kernel body + its launch config, not the
host side: a verbatim stock-kernel transplant on this tree measures
1376.0 t/s @ d32768, and forcing r205's own body to the stock 4x8 config
gives only 375 vs the stock kernel's 463 at d131072 -- identical config,
the body is the whole gap.

Two independent levers in fattn-tile.cuh, both RDNA2-only (compile-time
RDNA2 macro for the first, GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_RDNA2 for the second):

1. q_global threshold 16 -> 64 (11 sites: the two kernel-side conditions,
   the Q_tmp_count stub condition, 7 launcher q_h2 args, 1 comment).
   The global-half2 Q path is only worth it at >= 64 columns; at the
   prefill config (16x2 = 32 cols) it makes the kernel re-read Q from
   global per K-tile pass and the kernel spills 140-145 VGPRs.  Below
   64 cols Q goes back to LDS: 0 spills.

2. rdna_cap_ncols2: lifted for DKQ == 256 (D=128 keeps the cap).  The
   cap's comment claims the D=256 ncols2>=4 variants "overflow the
   register file (occupancy query returns 0 -> abort)"; measured 4x8
   D=256 launches run fine on this box/toolchain, including native q8_0
   KV (no abort) -- the manual WGP occupancy fallback keeps >= 1 block
   resident even when the kernel spills scratch.  Lifting the cap lets
   BOTH prefill and decode take the GQA-8 fold: KV read once per block
   instead of 4x.

Validation (slavap-pd-7900, Radeon Pro V620 gfx1030 = Rocm2, Qwen3.6-35B-
A3B-UD-IQ4_XS, -lm dio -b 8192 -ub 2048 -fa 1 -r 1):

  test              r205 release   this block   delta
  pp2048 @ d0        2330.2         2347.1        ~0
  pp2048 @ d32768    1041.0         1106.5       +6.3%
  pp2048 @ d131072    368.2          411.7      +11.8%
  tg256 @ d131072     50.9           58.9       +16.0%

- greedy token sanity: two -fa 1 runs (-s 42 -n 30) byte-identical to
  each other and to -fa 0
- RDNA3 (gfx1100, Rocm0) pp/tg vs the pre-fix build: within 0.4% on all
  four rows
- stock-kernel A/B (not shipped): the verbatim stock 4x8 body on this
  tree measures 1376.0 t/s @ d32768 but aborts at d131072 (HSA memory
  aperture; the stock body predates this tree's launcher contract).
  The residual of THIS block vs stock at 32k (1106.5 vs 1231.7) is the
  r205 4x8 body's register pressure (256 VGPR + 488B scratch vs stock's
  212 VGPR / 0B) -- a separate body-trimming follow-up, not a launch
  hazard.

